    "done_when": "Continue from 331311bb9, whose driver under docs/figures/centroid-constrained-oracle-solve/certificate-ladder-110-300/ binds the support mode in every typed request, forwards nested solve calls and resolves its path from the submit tree. Its CPU preflight cannot pass because an exact-clip solve aborts in LLVM section-memory allocation on CPU, so do not preflight on CPU. ONE H200 job (betelgeuse, gpu_0003_grpA, one card, 8 CPUs, --mem=128G, --time=02:00:00, TMPDIR=/tmp in submit and payload, the shared interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python without uv, RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 sbatch; titan only if still PENDING on resources after a minute) begins with a preflight inside the job: the weak -110 exact and whole-cell requests through the same code path with a one-trip budget, logging the realised support mode of each and exiting nonzero before the ladder if they match or if either call fails. It then runs weak, moderate and strong at -110 and -300 cells, both arms, from the production seed, each row persisted as it lands with its accepted Newton promotions and, when none, the solver history field that says why. Once admitted, commit, park with the sacct probe and job id, and end the turn. The resumed turn renders the twelve line-contour panels (shared levels, both null sets, wall, residual and converged flag in the caption), rewrites the report table with the clause verdicts, accepted promotions per row and whether exact and control differ, and updates the fragment. A failing row is reported as measured; no source under nova/ is edited.",
